# Knowledge Quality Rule

When updating role memory or shared lessons, entries must be structured and evidence-oriented.

Required fields per KB entry:
- `Context`
- `Action`
- `Outcome`
- `Evidence`
- `Reuse-tag`

Quality policy:
- Write concise, reusable lessons; avoid generic diary-style updates.
- Never include secrets or credentials in KB files.
- Prefer patterns that can be reused across projects.

Freshness policy:
- If a role has no meaningful KB update after major work cycles, PM must trigger reminder/escalation.
- Repeated defects should produce preventive KB entries linked to defect records.
